# Sheet spec sync after every change

When you fix or learn anything about a **named 619 sheet build** (compiler,
executor, VBA draw path, engineer QA correction, visual gotcha):

## Required in the same effort (do not defer)

1. **`Data/sheet-specs/<sheet>.json`** — encode anything the compiler,
   executor, or agent must obey on the affected item (`signs.items[]`,
   `symbols.items[]`, `representation`, `annotationStyle`, notes fields).
2. **`Data/sheet-specs/<sheet>.build.md`** (or create/update the playbook
   `sheet.buildGuide` points at) — human tip + Do-not / common-failure row.
3. **`dev-notes/agent-log.md`** — cross-tool bridge (Cursor ↔ Claude Code).

The in-MicroStation WZTC agent loads `buildGuide` from
`get_sheet_requirements` / `get_sheet_build_guide`. If the tip lives only in
chat or only in `agent-log.md`, the **next agent turn will miss it**.

## Authority reminder

Official PDF → sheet JSON → build playbook → chat hints. Updating JSON/playbook
is how a live fix becomes sheet-first authority for the agent.

## Anti-patterns (forbidden)

- Shipping a code fix and saying “document later”
- Logging only in `agent-log.md` without JSON/playbook
- Leaving an outdated playbook tip that contradicts the fix (edit or replace
  the old Do-not row — do not leave both)

## Scope

Applies to named-sheet work (619-xxx). General CAD one-offs still use
`agent-log.md` when non-obvious; no sheet JSON required if no sheet was
involved.
